{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917506832},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Find how many farmers markets the U.S. has\n2. Find the total U.S. residents (census data)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to 4 decimal places\n4. Provide one confident sentence with only verified facts\n\nI need to follow the xorq analyst procedure:\n1. Orient - check for semantic models first\n2. Get the data into the catalog if not already there\n3. Compute values with xorq_select\n4. Verify with xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by checking if there's already a catalog and semantic models.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you answer this by getting the data into the catalog and computing the verified metric. Let me start by orienting to the existing catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012g3FXwHsmQzPCpJUTJau3c","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Enm3hSxo4mCer4v4XtCSPQ","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":293,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8302,"totalTokens":8605,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0014650000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0103775,"total":0.0118525},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":146},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":17869